<title>USA: U.S. Sept retail sales rose 0.7 percent.</title>
<headline>U.S. Sept retail sales rose 0.7 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce Department seasonally adjusted data on U.S. retail sales.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:  Sept	Aug--Rev from    Sept96/95</p>
<p> Retail Sales	    0.7     -0.2     0.2	   4.7</p>
<p> Excluding Autos	 0.4     -0.5     0.2	   3.8</p>
<p> Auto Sales		1.7	0.5     0.1	   7.7</p>
<p> Durable Goods	   0.9     -0.1     0.3	   7.0</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods	0.6     -0.3     0.1	   3.2</p>
<p> Furniture Stores     -0.3	1.0    -0.2	   3.6</p>
<p> Building Materials    0.1     -2.2    -0.7	   7.6</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs: Sept     Aug---Rev from   July--Rev from</p>
<p> Retail Sales	 205.71   204.25   205.00   204.72   204.66</p>
<p> Excluding Autos    154.90   154.28   155.33   154.99   155.07</p>
<p> Auto Sales	    50.81    49.98    49.67    49.73    49.60</p>
<p> Durable Goods	 84.18    83.47    83.78    83.54    83.55</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods   121.53   120.78   121.22   121.18   121.11</p>
<p> Furniture Stores    11.48    11.52    11.33    11.40    11.35</p>
<p> Building Materials  11.14    11.13    11.39    11.38    11.46</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:  Sept	Aug--Rev from   Sept 96/95</p>
<p> General Merchandise   0.3	0.8     0.7	   4.2</p>
<p> Department Stores     0.5	0.9     0.9	   4.3</p>
<p> Food Stores	     1.2     -0.5    -0.7	   4.1</p>
<p> Grocery Stores	  1.2     -0.5    -0.7	   4.1</p>
<p> Gas Stations	    0.6     -0.8    -0.9	   5.6</p>
<p> Apparel Stores	 -0.1     -0.5     1.0	   0.9</p>
<p> Eat/Drink Places	0.5     -0.7    -0.4	   0.1</p>
<p> Drug Stores	    -0.3	1.1     0.4	   5.6</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs: Sept     Aug---Rev from    July--Rev from</p>
<p> General Merch.	26.02    25.95    25.92     25.75   25.74</p>
<p> Department Stores   20.28    20.17    20.16     20.00   19.98</p>
<p> Food Stores	   35.65    35.24    35.17     35.40   35.41</p>
<p> Grocery Stores	33.78    33.38    33.30     33.55   33.54</p>
<p> Gas Stations	  12.95    12.87    12.92     12.97   13.03</p>
<p> Apparel Stores	 9.36     9.37     9.51	9.41    9.42</p>
<p> Eat/Drink Places    19.65    19.54    19.44     19.69   19.51</p>
<p> Drug Stores	    7.49     7.52     7.46	7.44    7.44</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected September retail sales to rise 0.2 percent, and sales excluding autos to up 0.3 percent.  </p>
<p>The department said the 0.5 percent drop in August retail sales excluding autos was the largest since a 0.6 percent decline in October 1995.</p>
<p>The department revised July retail sales to a 0.2 percent rise from a 0.1 percent rise. It revised July sales excluding autos to up 0.1 percent from a 0.2 percent increase, and July auto sales to a 0.2 percent rise from unchanged.</p>
